<title>USA: Res-Care completes Premier acquisition.</title>
<headline>Res-Care completes Premier acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE, Ky. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Res-Care Inc on Tuesday said it completed the acquisition of Premier Rehabilitation Centers, a provider of services for patients with acquired brain injury and related neurological disorders.</p>
<p>The transaction, announced on December 11, involved the exchange of 409,250 shares of Res-Care common stock. It is to be treated as a pooling of interests.</p>
<p>Res-Care shares were up 1/2 at 18-1/4 in early afternoon trading on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Premier generates annual revenues of $6.5 million.</p>
<p>Res-Care provides services for persons with mental retardation and other developmental disabilites.</p>
</text>
